IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division C, "Employees and Employers": sections 21, 21.01 and 21.1.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. No point of view is taken here.
--
-- Section 21 puts one duty on an employer: deduct the employee's contribution from the remuneration, and
-- remit it with the employer's own contribution to the Receiver General. The rest of the section says what
-- follows from not doing so: liability for the whole amount, interest, a penalty, and a way to recover a
-- missed deduction from a later payment. Section 21.01 treats a deduction taken on an overpayment made by
-- mistake as never taken. Section 21.1 makes the directors of a corporate employer liable with it.
--
-- Every rule is constitutive (BOOLEAN, NUMBER or DATE). A "must" is the BOOLEAN that the duty arises; the
-- consequence of not performing it is a separate rule, as the phrasebook (5.1, 5.2, 5.7) recommends.
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a rate is a fraction (3% is 0.03); a day is a DATE.
--
-- Facts the text takes from provisions outside this piece are plain inputs with a comment "out of range".
-- Terms the interpretation section defines are the keel's: `s 2(1) — an employer`, `s 2(1) — an employee`.

§ `Division C -- Employees and Employers`

§§ `s 21 -- the employment relationship (nouns)`

-- The facts a witness could state about who pays whom. The employer and employee of section 21 are the
-- section 2(1) terms; the keel works those out from these facts (see the two helpers below).
-- "pensionable employment" is section 6(1), which piece cp1 encodes, so it is a plain input here.
-- src:41 | employee includes an officer; (employé)
-- src:42 | employer means a person liable to pay salary, wages or other remuneration in relation to employment, and, in relation to an officer, includes the person from whom the officer receives their remuneration; (employeur)
-- src:43 | employment means the state of being employed under an express or implied contract of service or apprenticeship, and includes the tenure of an office; (emploi)
@ref Act s 2(1) "employee", "employer", "employment" (src:41-43)
DECLARE `cp2 Employment relationship` HAS
    `payer is liable to pay salary, wages or other remuneration in relation to the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payee is employed under an express or implied contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payee holds an office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payee, as an officer, receives their remuneration from the payer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employment is pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: subsection 6(1) (piece cp1)

-- none: a helper that asks the keel whether the payer is an "employer" of the payee (section 2(1)).
@ref Act s 2(1) "employer" (src:42)
GIVEN relationship IS A `cp2 Employment relationship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payer is an employer of the payee` relationship MEANS
    `s 2(1) — an employer`
        (relationship's `payer is liable to pay salary, wages or other remuneration in relation to the employment`)
        (relationship's `payee holds an office`)
        (relationship's `payee, as an officer, receives their remuneration from the payer`)

-- none: a helper that asks the keel whether the payee is an "employee" of the payer (section 2(1)).
@ref Act s 2(1) "employee", "employment" (src:41-43)
GIVEN relationship IS A `cp2 Employment relationship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payee is an employee of the payer` relationship MEANS
    `s 2(1) — an employee`
        (`s 2(1) — employment`
            (relationship's `payee is employed under an express or implied contract of service or apprenticeship`)
            (relationship's `payee holds an office`))
        (relationship's `payee holds an office`)

§§ `s 21(1) -- deduct and remit`

-- src:590 | Amount to be deducted and remitted by employer
-- src:591 | 21 (1) Every employer paying remuneration to an employee employed by the employer at any time in pensionable employment shall deduct from that remuneration as or on account of the employee’s contributions for the year in which the remuneration in respect of the pensionable employment is paid to the employee any amount that is determined in accordance with prescribed rules and shall remit that amount, together with any amount that is prescribed with respect to the contributions required to be made by the employer under this Act, to the Receiver General at any time that is prescribed and, if at that prescribed time the employer is a prescribed person, the remittance shall be made to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution (within the meaning that would be assigned by the definition financial institution in subsection 190(1) of the Income Tax Act if that definition were read without reference to its paragraphs (d) and (e)).
@ref Act s 21(1) (src:590-591)
GIVEN relationship IS A `cp2 Employment relationship`
      `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) — the employer must deduct from the remuneration` relationship `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment` MEANS
        `the payer is an employer of the payee` relationship
    AND `the payee is an employee of the payer` relationship
    AND `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment`
    AND relationship's `employment is pensionable employment`

@ref Act s 21(1) (src:590-591)
GIVEN relationship IS A `cp2 Employment relationship`
      `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount determined in accordance with the prescribed rules` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: the rules prescribed for subsection 21(1), Regulations Part I (piece cr1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(1) — the amount the employer must deduct` relationship `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment` `the amount determined in accordance with the prescribed rules` MEANS
    IF `s 21(1) — the employer must deduct from the remuneration` relationship `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment`
    THEN `the amount determined in accordance with the prescribed rules`
    ELSE 0

@ref Act s 21(1) (src:590-591)
GIVEN relationship IS A `cp2 Employment relationship`
      `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount determined in accordance with the prescribed rules` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount prescribed with respect to the contributions required to be made by the employer` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: Regulations Part I (piece cr1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(1) — the amount the employer must remit` relationship `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment` `the amount determined in accordance with the prescribed rules` `the amount prescribed with respect to the contributions required to be made by the employer` MEANS
    IF `s 21(1) — the employer must deduct from the remuneration` relationship `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment`
    THEN `the amount determined in accordance with the prescribed rules` PLUS `the amount prescribed with respect to the contributions required to be made by the employer`
    ELSE 0

-- Where the remittance goes: to the Receiver General, or, for a prescribed person at the prescribed time,
-- to the Receiver General's account at a financial institution.
@ref Act s 21(1) (src:590-591)
DECLARE `cp2 Place of remittance` IS ONE OF
    `the amount is remitted to the Receiver General`
    `the amount is remitted to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution`

@ref Act s 21(1) (src:590-591)
GIVEN `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the persons prescribed for subsection 21(1), Regulations section 8.2 (piece cr1)
GIVETH A `cp2 Place of remittance`
`s 21(1) — where the employer must remit` `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time` MEANS
    IF `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time`
    THEN `the amount is remitted to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution`
    ELSE `the amount is remitted to the Receiver General`

-- src:592 | Exception — remittance to financial institution
-- src:593 | (1.1) For the purpose of subsection (1), a prescribed person referred to in that subsection is deemed to have remitted an amount to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution referred to in that subsection if the prescribed person has remitted the amount to the Receiver General at least one day before the day on which the amount is due.
@ref Act s 21(1.1) (src:592-593)
GIVEN `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the amount was remitted to the Receiver General` IS A DATE
      `the day the amount is due` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(1.1) — the prescribed person is deemed to have remitted to the account at a financial institution` `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time` `the day the amount was remitted to the Receiver General` `the day the amount is due` MEANS
        `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time`
    AND (`the day the amount was remitted to the Receiver General` PLUS 1) AT MOST `the day the amount is due`

-- none: a helper that puts subsections (1) and (1.1) together. The remittance is in the manner required if the
-- employer is not a prescribed person (any remittance to the Receiver General), or paid into the account at a
-- financial institution, or deemed to have been by subsection (1.1).
@ref Act s 21(1), s 21(1.1) (src:590-593)
GIVEN `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount was remitted to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the amount was remitted to the Receiver General` IS A DATE
      `the day the amount is due` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) — the amount was remitted in the manner required` `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time` `the amount was remitted to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution` `the day the amount was remitted to the Receiver General` `the day the amount is due` MEANS
        (NOT `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time`)
    OR  `the amount was remitted to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution`
    OR  `s 21(1.1) — the prescribed person is deemed to have remitted to the account at a financial institution` `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time` `the day the amount was remitted to the Receiver General` `the day the amount is due`

§§ `s 21(2) and (3) -- liability for failing to deduct and remit, and its limit`

-- src:596 | Subsequent decision — limit on liability
-- src:597 | (3) An employer is not liable for any amount that the employer fails to deduct as required by this Act from the remuneration of an employee, or for any interest or penalties for that failure, if
-- src:598 | (a) the employer is informed in writing in a ruling under section 26.1 that the employer is not required to make the deduction;
-- src:599 | (b) the ruling is not based on information provided by the employer to the Minister that was incorrect in a material particular; and
-- src:600 | (c) it is subsequently decided under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 that the deduction should have been made.
@ref Act s 21(3) (src:596-600)
GIVEN `the employer is informed in writing in a ruling under section 26.1 that it is not required to make the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ruling is based on information provided by the employer to the Minister that was incorrect in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is subsequently decided under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 that the deduction should have been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(3) — the employer is not liable for the amount it failed to deduct, or for interest or penalties` `the employer is informed in writing in a ruling under section 26.1 that it is not required to make the deduction` `the ruling is based on information provided by the employer to the Minister that was incorrect in a material particular` `it is subsequently decided under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 that the deduction should have been made` MEANS
        `the employer is informed in writing in a ruling under section 26.1 that it is not required to make the deduction`
    AND (NOT `the ruling is based on information provided by the employer to the Minister that was incorrect in a material particular`)
    AND `it is subsequently decided under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 that the deduction should have been made`

-- src:594 | Liability for failure to deduct and remit
-- src:595 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), every employer who fails to deduct and remit an amount from the remuneration of an employee as and when required under subsection (1) is liable to pay to Her Majesty the whole amount that should have been deducted and remitted from the time it should have been deducted.
@ref Act s 21(2) (src:594-595)
GIVEN `the employer failed to deduct and remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(2) — the employer is liable to pay Her Majesty the whole amount` `the employer failed to deduct and remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1)` `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` MEANS
        `the employer failed to deduct and remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1)`
    AND (NOT `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)`)

@ref Act s 21(2) (src:594-595)
GIVEN `the employer failed to deduct and remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount that should have been deducted and remitted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(2) — the amount the employer is liable to pay Her Majesty` `the employer failed to deduct and remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1)` `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` `the amount that should have been deducted and remitted` MEANS
    IF `s 21(2) — the employer is liable to pay Her Majesty the whole amount` `the employer failed to deduct and remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1)` `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)`
    THEN `the amount that should have been deducted and remitted`
    ELSE 0

-- "from the time it should have been deducted": the liability runs from the day of the payment of
-- remuneration out of which the deduction was due.
@ref Act s 21(2) (src:594-595)
GIVEN `the time the amount should have been deducted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(2) — the time from which the liability to pay runs` `the time the amount should have been deducted` MEANS
    `the time the amount should have been deducted`

-- src:601 | Payment and deemed notification
-- src:602 | (3.1) Once the decision under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 is communicated to the employer, the employer is liable without interest or penalties under this Act to pay any contribution required to be paid by the employer with respect to the employee. On payment by the employer of any amount as or on account of that contribution, the employee is deemed to have notified the Minister as required by subsection 15(1.1), 15.1(1.1) or 15.2(1.1) of the employer’s failure to deduct the amount of that contribution from the remuneration of the employee.
@ref Act s 21(3.1) (src:601-602)
GIVEN `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 has been communicated to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(3.1) — the employer is liable, without interest or penalties, to pay the contribution required of the employer` `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` `the decision under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 has been communicated to the employer` MEANS
        `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)`
    AND `the decision under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 has been communicated to the employer`

@ref Act s 21(3.1) (src:601-602)
GIVEN `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 has been communicated to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contribution required to be paid by the employer with respect to the employee` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 9 (piece cp1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(3.1) — the contribution the employer must pay, without interest or penalties` `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` `the decision under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 has been communicated to the employer` `the contribution required to be paid by the employer with respect to the employee` MEANS
    IF `s 21(3.1) — the employer is liable, without interest or penalties, to pay the contribution required of the employer` `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` `the decision under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 has been communicated to the employer`
    THEN `the contribution required to be paid by the employer with respect to the employee`
    ELSE 0

-- The second sentence of subsection (3.1): payment of any amount on the contribution is a deemed notice, by the
-- employee, to the Minister that the employer did not deduct. The notice "required by subsection 15(1.1),
-- 15.1(1.1) or 15.2(1.1)" is cp1's; here it is only the thing deemed to have been given.
@ref Act s 21(3.1) (src:601-602)
GIVEN `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 has been communicated to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has paid an amount as or on account of that contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(3.1) — the employee is deemed to have notified the Minister of the employer's failure to deduct` `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` `the decision under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 has been communicated to the employer` `the employer has paid an amount as or on account of that contribution` MEANS
        `s 21(3.1) — the employer is liable, without interest or penalties, to pay the contribution required of the employer` `the employer is not liable under subsection 21(3)` `the decision under subsection 27.2(3) or section 28 has been communicated to the employer`
    AND `the employer has paid an amount as or on account of that contribution`

§§ `s 21(4) and (5) -- recovering a missed deduction, and the employee's deemed receipt`

-- src:603 | Deduction from subsequent payment of remuneration
-- src:604 | (4) Any employer who fails to deduct an amount that is required by subsection (1) to be deducted from a payment of remuneration to an employee may deduct an amount equal to the amount from any subsequent payment of remuneration made to the employee within 12 months after the making of the payment from which the amount was required to be deducted, but no employer may deduct from a payment of remuneration made to an employee, in addition to the amount required by subsection (1) to be deducted therefrom, any amount with respect to more than one such amount that the employer previously failed to deduct.
@ref Act s 21(4) (src:603-604)
GIVEN `the employer failed to deduct an amount required by subsection 21(1) from a payment of remuneration to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the payment from which the amount was required to be deducted` IS A DATE
      `the day of the subsequent payment of remuneration` IS A DATE
      `the number of earlier missed amounts the employer now deducts from the subsequent payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(4) — the employer may deduct the missed amount from a subsequent payment of remuneration` `the employer failed to deduct an amount required by subsection 21(1) from a payment of remuneration to the employee` `the day of the payment from which the amount was required to be deducted` `the day of the subsequent payment of remuneration` `the number of earlier missed amounts the employer now deducts from the subsequent payment` MEANS
        `the employer failed to deduct an amount required by subsection 21(1) from a payment of remuneration to the employee`
    AND `a date is within a time limit after a start date`
            `the day of the subsequent payment of remuneration`
            `the day of the payment from which the amount was required to be deducted`
            (`a number of months` WITH `number of months` IS 12)
    AND `the number of earlier missed amounts the employer now deducts from the subsequent payment` EQUALS 1

-- src:605 | Amount deducted deemed received by employee
-- src:606 | (5) Where an amount has been deducted under subsection (1), it shall be deemed for all purposes to have been received at that time by the employee to whom the remuneration was payable.
@ref Act s 21(5) (src:605-606)
GIVEN `an amount has been deducted under subsection 21(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(5) — the employee is deemed to have received the amount deducted` `an amount has been deducted under subsection 21(1)` MEANS
    `an amount has been deducted under subsection 21(1)`

@ref Act s 21(5) (src:605-606)
GIVEN `the time the amount was deducted under subsection 21(1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(5) — the time at which the employee is deemed to have received the amount` `the time the amount was deducted under subsection 21(1)` MEANS
    `the time the amount was deducted under subsection 21(1)`

§§ `s 21(6) and (7) -- interest and penalty for failing to remit`

-- The text says "interest ... at the prescribed rate computed from the day on which the employer was so required
-- to remit the amount to the day of remittance". It does not say how a day is counted or whether the interest
-- compounds. Taken here (fork F2): simple interest, the days from the day required to the day of remittance,
-- counted as the difference of the two dates, over a 365-day year. The prescribed rate is Regulations
-- paragraph 36(2)(a), which changes each quarter; a caller whose period crosses a quarter splits it.
-- src:607 | Interest on amounts not remitted
-- src:608 | (6) Where an employer has failed to remit to the Receiver General an amount that the employer was required to remit at the time when he was required to do so, the employer shall pay to the Receiver General interest on that amount at the prescribed rate computed from the day on which the employer was so required to remit the amount to the day of remittance of the amount to the Receiver General.
@ref Act s 21(6) (src:607-608)
GIVEN `the amount the employer failed to remit at the time required` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the amount was required to be remitted` IS A DATE
      `the day the amount was remitted` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed rate of interest per annum` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: Regulations section 36 (piece cr1); a fraction per annum, 5% is 0.05
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(6) — the interest the employer must pay the Receiver General` `the amount the employer failed to remit at the time required` `the day the amount was required to be remitted` `the day the amount was remitted` `the prescribed rate of interest per annum` MEANS
    IF `the day the amount was remitted` AT MOST `the day the amount was required to be remitted`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the amount the employer failed to remit at the time required`
         TIMES `the prescribed rate of interest per annum`
         TIMES ((Day `the day the amount was remitted` MINUS Day `the day the amount was required to be remitted`) DIVIDED BY 365)

-- src:609 | Penalty for failure to remit
-- src:610 | (7) Every employer who in a calendar year fails to remit to the Receiver General an amount that the employer is required to remit at the time when he is required to do so is liable to a penalty of
-- src:611 | (a) subject to paragraph (b), if
-- src:612 | (i) the Receiver General receives that amount on or before the day it was due, but that amount is not paid in the manner required, three per cent of that amount,
-- src:613 | (ii) the Receiver General receives that amount
-- src:614 | (A) no more than three days after it was due, three per cent of that amount,
-- src:615 | (B) more than three days and no more than five days after it was due, five per cent of that amount, or
-- src:616 | (C) more than five days and no more than seven days after it was due, seven per cent of that amount, or
-- src:617 | (iii) that amount is not paid or remitted on or before the seventh day after it was due, ten per cent of that amount; or
-- src:618 | (b) where at the time of the failure a penalty under this subsection was payable by the employer in respect of an amount that the employer was required to remit during the year and the failure was made knowingly or under circumstances amounting to gross negligence, twenty per cent of the amount.
@ref Act s 21(7) (src:609-618)
GIVEN `the day the amount was due` IS A DATE
      `the day the Receiver General received the amount, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the amount was paid in the manner required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(7) — the employer failed to remit the amount at the time required` `the day the amount was due` `the day the Receiver General received the amount, if it has` `the amount was paid in the manner required` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the Receiver General received the amount, if it has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST received THEN received GREATER THAN `the day the amount was due` OR (NOT `the amount was paid in the manner required`)

-- The rate is a fraction of the amount that the employer was required to remit.
-- (b) wins over (a): "(a) subject to paragraph (b)". Within (a): received on or before the due day but not in the
-- manner required, or no more than three days late: 3%; four or five days: 5%; six or seven days: 7%; more
-- than seven days late or never: 10%.
@ref Act s 21(7) (src:609-618)
GIVEN `the day the amount was due` IS A DATE
      `the day the Receiver General received the amount, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the amount was paid in the manner required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a penalty under this subsection was payable by the employer in respect of an amount required to be remitted during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure was made knowingly or under circumstances amounting to gross negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(7) — the rate of the penalty for failing to remit` `the day the amount was due` `the day the Receiver General received the amount, if it has` `the amount was paid in the manner required` `a penalty under this subsection was payable by the employer in respect of an amount required to be remitted during the year` `the failure was made knowingly or under circumstances amounting to gross negligence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 21(7) — the employer failed to remit the amount at the time required` `the day the amount was due` `the day the Receiver General received the amount, if it has` `the amount was paid in the manner required`) THEN 0
        IF `a penalty under this subsection was payable by the employer in respect of an amount required to be remitted during the year` AND `the failure was made knowingly or under circumstances amounting to gross negligence` THEN 20%
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the day the Receiver General received the amount, if it has`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 10%
            WHEN JUST received THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF (Day received MINUS Day `the day the amount was due`) AT MOST 3 THEN 3%
                    IF (Day received MINUS Day `the day the amount was due`) AT MOST 5 THEN 5%
                    IF (Day received MINUS Day `the day the amount was due`) AT MOST 7 THEN 7%
                    OTHERWISE 10%

@ref Act s 21(7) (src:609-618)
GIVEN `the amount the employer was required to remit` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the amount was due` IS A DATE
      `the day the Receiver General received the amount, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the amount was paid in the manner required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a penalty under this subsection was payable by the employer in respect of an amount required to be remitted during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure was made knowingly or under circumstances amounting to gross negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(7) — the penalty for failing to remit` `the amount the employer was required to remit` `the day the amount was due` `the day the Receiver General received the amount, if it has` `the amount was paid in the manner required` `a penalty under this subsection was payable by the employer in respect of an amount required to be remitted during the year` `the failure was made knowingly or under circumstances amounting to gross negligence` MEANS
    `the amount the employer was required to remit`
        TIMES `s 21(7) — the rate of the penalty for failing to remit` `the day the amount was due` `the day the Receiver General received the amount, if it has` `the amount was paid in the manner required` `a penalty under this subsection was payable by the employer in respect of an amount required to be remitted during the year` `the failure was made knowingly or under circumstances amounting to gross negligence`

§§ `s 21.01 -- an excess payment made by mistake`

-- src:619 | Excess payment — amount deemed not deducted
-- src:620 | 21.01 (1) Subject to subsection (2), an amount deducted by an employer under subsection 21(1) for a year after 2015 in respect of an excess payment that was paid — as a result of a clerical, administrative or system error — as remuneration to an employee in respect of pensionable employment is deemed not to have been deducted for the purposes of this Act if
-- src:621 | (a) before the end of the third year after the calendar year in which the amount was deducted,
-- src:622 | (i) the employer elects to have this section apply in respect of the amount, and
-- src:623 | (ii) the employee has repaid, or made an arrangement to repay, the employer;
-- src:624 | (b) the employer has not filed an information return correcting for the excess payment before making the election referred to in subparagraph (a)(i); and
-- src:625 | (c) any additional conditions specified by the Minister are met.
@ref Act s 21.01(1) (src:619-625)
GIVEN `the year of the deduction` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount deducted was on an excess payment paid as remuneration as a result of a clerical, administrative or system error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the employer elected to have section 21.01 apply, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the employee repaid or made an arrangement to repay the employer, if the employee has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the employer filed an information return correcting for the excess payment, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `any additional conditions specified by the Minister are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21.01(1) — the amount deducted is deemed not to have been deducted` `the year of the deduction` `the amount deducted was on an excess payment paid as remuneration as a result of a clerical, administrative or system error` `the day the employer elected to have section 21.01 apply, if it has` `the day the employee repaid or made an arrangement to repay the employer, if the employee has` `the day the employer filed an information return correcting for the excess payment, if it has` `any additional conditions specified by the Minister are met` MEANS
        `the year of the deduction` GREATER THAN 2015
    AND `the amount deducted was on an excess payment paid as remuneration as a result of a clerical, administrative or system error`
    AND `the last day for acting under section 21.01 has not passed on` `the year of the deduction` `the day the employer elected to have section 21.01 apply, if it has`
    AND `the last day for acting under section 21.01 has not passed on` `the year of the deduction` `the day the employee repaid or made an arrangement to repay the employer, if the employee has`
    AND `the employer has not filed a correcting information return before the election` `the day the employer elected to have section 21.01 apply, if it has` `the day the employer filed an information return correcting for the excess payment, if it has`
    AND `any additional conditions specified by the Minister are met`
    WHERE
        -- (a): "before the end of the third year after the calendar year in which the amount was deducted".
        -- Taken (fork F3): the last day of that third year is still before its end. An act that has not happened (NOTHING) is not before it.
        `the last day for acting under section 21.01 has not passed on` theYear whenDone MEANS
            CONSIDER whenDone
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d THEN d AT MOST (`s 2(1) — the last day of a year` (theYear PLUS 3))
        -- (b): "the employer has not filed an information return correcting for the excess payment before making the election".
        `the employer has not filed a correcting information return before the election` election filed MEANS
            CONSIDER election
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST e THEN
                CONSIDER filed
                WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                WHEN JUST f THEN f AT LEAST e

-- src:626 | Determination of amount
-- src:627 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the amount that is deemed not to have been deducted is the amount that was deducted by the employer or, if the amount determined by the following formula is less than the amount that was deducted by the employer, the amount determined by the formula
-- src:628 | A − B
-- src:629 | where
-- src:630 | A is the aggregate of all amounts that were deducted by the employer as the employee’s contributions for the year in question; and
-- src:631 | B is the aggregate of all amounts that would have been deducted by the employer as the employee’s contributions for that year had the employer not made the excess payment referred to in subsection (1).
@ref Act s 21.01(2) (src:626-631)
GIVEN `the amount that was deducted by the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of all amounts deducted by the employer as the employee's contributions for the year in question` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of all amounts that would have been deducted as the employee's contributions for that year had the employer not made the excess payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21.01(2) — the amount deemed not to have been deducted` `the amount that was deducted by the employer` `the aggregate of all amounts deducted by the employer as the employee's contributions for the year in question` `the aggregate of all amounts that would have been deducted as the employee's contributions for that year had the employer not made the excess payment` MEANS
    min `the amount that was deducted by the employer`
        (`the aggregate of all amounts deducted by the employer as the employee's contributions for the year in question` MINUS `the aggregate of all amounts that would have been deducted as the employee's contributions for that year had the employer not made the excess payment`)

§§ `s 21.1 -- directors of a corporate employer`

-- src:632 | Liability
-- src:633 | 21.1 (1) If an employer who fails to deduct or remit an amount as and when required under subsection 21(1) is a corporation, the persons who were the directors of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred are jointly and severally or solidarily liable, together with the corporation, to pay to Her Majesty that amount and any interest or penalties relating to it.
@ref Act s 21.1(1) (src:632-633)
GIVEN `the employer that failed to deduct or remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1) is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21.1(1) — the director is jointly and severally liable with the corporation` `the employer that failed to deduct or remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1) is a corporation` `the person was a director of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred` MEANS
        `the employer that failed to deduct or remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1) is a corporation`
    AND `the person was a director of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred`

@ref Act s 21.1(1) (src:632-633)
GIVEN `the employer that failed to deduct or remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1) is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the corporation failed to deduct or remit` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest relating to that amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the penalties relating to that amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21.1(1) — the amount for which the director is liable to Her Majesty with the corporation` `the employer that failed to deduct or remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1) is a corporation` `the person was a director of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred` `the amount the corporation failed to deduct or remit` `the interest relating to that amount` `the penalties relating to that amount` MEANS
    IF `s 21.1(1) — the director is jointly and severally liable with the corporation` `the employer that failed to deduct or remit the amount as and when required under subsection 21(1) is a corporation` `the person was a director of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred`
    THEN `the amount the corporation failed to deduct or remit` PLUS `the interest relating to that amount` PLUS `the penalties relating to that amount`
    ELSE 0

-- Subsection (2) applies subsections 227.1(2) to (7) of the Income Tax Act "with such modifications as the
-- circumstances require". That Act is not among the texts this encoding reads, so what those subsections
-- allow (a limit on time, a defence of care) is a supplied fact (fork F4).
-- src:634 | Application of Income Tax Act provisions
-- src:635 | (2) Subsections 227.1(2) to (7) of the Income Tax Act apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of a director of a corporation referred to in subsection (1).
@ref Act s 21.1(2) (src:634-635)
GIVEN `the director is jointly and severally liable under subsection 21.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a limit or defence in subsections 227.1(2) to (7) of the Income Tax Act, as modified, relieves the director` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the Income Tax Act, which is not deposited
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21.1(2) — the director is liable after the Income Tax Act provisions applied by this subsection` `the director is jointly and severally liable under subsection 21.1(1)` `a limit or defence in subsections 227.1(2) to (7) of the Income Tax Act, as modified, relieves the director` MEANS
        `the director is jointly and severally liable under subsection 21.1(1)`
    AND (NOT `a limit or defence in subsections 227.1(2) to (7) of the Income Tax Act, as modified, relieves the director`)

-- src:636 | Assessment provisions applicable to directors
-- src:637 | (3) The provisions of this Act respecting the assessment of an employer for an amount payable by the employer under this Act and respecting the rights and obligations of an employer so assessed apply in respect of a director of a corporation in respect of an amount payable by the director under subsection (1) in the same manner and to the same extent as if the director were the employer referred to in those provisions.
@ref Act s 21.1(3) (src:636-637)
GIVEN `the director is jointly and severally liable under subsection 21.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21.1(3) — the assessment provisions and the rights of an assessed employer apply to the director` `the director is jointly and severally liable under subsection 21.1(1)` MEANS
    `the director is jointly and severally liable under subsection 21.1(1)`
